{"symbol":"SNK.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T19:57:46Z","info":{"address1":"ul. Przemyska 24","city":"Sanok","zip":"38-500","country":"Poland","phone":"48 13 465 4444","website":"https://www.sanokrubber.com","industry":"Auto Parts","industryKey":"auto-parts","industryDisp":"Auto Parts","sector":"Consumer Cyclical","sectorKey":"consumer-cyclical","sectorDisp":"Consumer Cyclical","longBusinessSummary":"Sanok Rubber Company Spólka Akcyjna engages in the production and sale of rubber products in Poland, Germany, France, Finland, Hungary, Ukraine, and Belarus. The company operates through five segments: Automotive, Construction, Agriculture and Industry, Rubber Mixtures, and Other. It offers rubber, rubber-metal, rubber-plastic, and elastomer products; thermoplastic TPEs for body sealing and car suspension systems, as well as exhaust system suspensions; sealing systems used in the production of window and door joinery, and gutter and ventilation systems; and self-adhesive seals used for sealing in installed joinery and aluminum substructures for ventilated facades. The company also provides V-belts and accessories under the Harvest Belts, Garden Belts, Vege Belts, and OptimumPro brands; stoppers for closing glass vials and plastic packaging with antibiotics, infusion fluids, and blood products; plungers for disposable syringes; and rubber products for household appliances, industrial hoses, and molded products for protecting industrial equipment against wear and corrosion. In addition, it is involved in the provision of repairs of machines and devices, sanatorium, recreation, and industrial services; and manufacturing of equipment to produce rubber and plastic products. The company was formerly known as Stomil Sanok S.A. and changed its name to Sanok Rubber Company Spólka Akcyjna in November 2015. Sanok Rubber Company Spólka Akcyjna was founded in 1932 and is headquartered in Sanok, Poland.","fullTimeEmployees":3099,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. 